  "result": "Excellent! I've successfully implemented payment terms support. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/errors.js** \u2014 Added `TERMS_INVALID` error code for unsupported payment terms.\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Enhanced `createInvoice()` with:\n   - Optional `terms` parameter (defaults to `'NET30'`)\n   - Support for three term types:\n     - `'NET14'` \u2014 due 14 days after issue date\n     - `'NET30'` \u2014 due 30 days after issue date (default)\n     - `'EOM'` \u2014 due on the last day of the invoice month\n   - Helper function `calculateDueDate()` to compute the due date\n   - Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` fields\n   - Returns `TERMS_INVALID` for unknown terms\n   - Terms and due date are preserved when issuing, adding, or removing invoice lines\n\n3. **test/invoices.test.js** \u2014 Added 16 new tests covering:\n   - Default NET30 behavior\n   - NET14 and NET30 calculations\n   - EOM calculations including edge cases (February in leap/non-leap years, December, month boundaries)\n   - Error handling for invalid, empty, and lowercase terms\n   - Terms preservation through invoice operations\n\nAll 149 tests pass, including the 16 new ones for terms functionality.",
